  "question": {
    "text": "If number of aldose, ketose, furanose and pyranose units present in maltose are p, q, r, s respectively. Find the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math><br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/a8814cfc-1094-4da9-8cdf-f99f03c31a62.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:3.525in;height:1.75833in\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Monomer of maltose is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math> -D-glucopyranose. It is disaciharide, so 2 aldose and 2 pyranose forms are present in maltose.<br />Hence, p = 2, q = 0, r = 0 and s = 2<br />So, sum of p + q + r + s = 2 + 0 + 0 + 2 = 4.",
    "image": null
  },
